hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1164","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He prays thirteen rak’ahs at night.” It was narrated to us by Al-San’ani Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, it was narrated to us by Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas By the same token"
"1165","Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Saad He heard Jabir bin Abdullah: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed thirteen rak’ahs after dark.”"
